<title>HUNGARY: Fotex buys own shares on OTC market.</title>
<headline>Fotex buys own shares on OTC market.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian retail chain Fotex Rt said on Friday it had bought one million own shares on the over-the-counter (OTC) market.</p>
<p>In a separate statement, also published in the official bourse gazette, Fotex's major shareholder Blackburn International Inc said it had bought three million Fotex stocks, also on the OTC market.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, Fotex Property Developer said it had given a commission (to a brokerage) for the sale of 250,000 Fotex stocks.</p>
<p>On Thursday on the Budapest Stock Exchange Fotex shares finished at 88 forints, down three.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
